e routes connecting the Adriatic Sea and the Danube, this city has been a melting pot of various cultures and influences, notably during the Roman Empire when it was known as Emona. The city emerged as a significant center for commerce, education, and governance, reflecting the broader historical changes that shaped the region throughout the Classical era and beyond.

